greCy's parts have different licenses, because its training data do:

Code (scripts/, configs/, project.yml)   MIT, below
grc_proiel_* models (from 3.8.2)         CC BY-NC-SA 4.0
grc_perseus_* models (from 3.8.2)        CC BY-NC-SA 4.0
grc_ner_trf model (from 3.8.2)           CC BY-SA 4.0
UD Ancient Greek PROIEL treebank and     CC BY-NC-SA 3.0
  its corpora                            (assets/UD_Ancient_Greek-PROIEL/LICENSE.txt)
UD Ancient Greek Perseus treebank and    CC BY-NC-SA 2.5
  its corpora                            (assets/UD_Ancient_Greek-Perseus/LICENSE.txt)
NEReus NER corpus                        CC BY-SA 4.0
  (https://github.com/jmyerston/NEReus)
Floret vectors used to train the large   CC BY 4.0
  models (https://zenodo.org/record/5733373)

CC BY-NC-SA 4.0: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/
CC BY-SA 4.0: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/

The PROIEL and Perseus models can't be used commercially, because their
treebanks don't allow it. ikelos and Morpheus are a separate dependency under
MPL-2.0.

